# Level 6: Clocktower Core
# One vast mechanism fills the back wall. Stop the three marked drive gears when
# their corresponding hands reach XII; a mistimed gear can be restarted.
script clocktower_core
bounds 0 0 1600 900
playerStart 64 770
clockFace 800 355 210

# Enclosed single-screen clock chamber.
solid 0 0 1600 32
solid 0 32 32 788
solid 1568 32 32 788
solid 0 820 1600 80

# TIME / GOING TRAIN - a compact planted train rising from the winding barrel
# through the center, third, and fourth wheels to the escapement. Small pinions
# share the major wheel arbors, as they would between a real movement's plates.
layer background
gear spur mounted vertical 250 540 96 7.7 120 8 -8 -8 none
gear ratchet mounted horizontal 250 540 58 4.6 60 18 -8 -8 none
gear spur mounted vertical 412 490 72 5.8 90 14 0 0 none
gear lantern mounted horizontal 412 490 25 2.0 12 35 24 24 none
gear spur mounted vertical 500 410 56 4.5 75 8 0 0 none
gear lantern mounted horizontal 500 410 22 1.8 10 10 -36 -36 none
gear spur mounted vertical 530 315 44 3.5 60 22 0 0 none
gear escape mounted vertical 500 220 50 4.0 30 0 0 0 none
gear sector mounted vertical 555 155 30 2.4 24 130 0 0 none

# MOTION WORK / DIAL TRAIN - cannon pinion, minute wheel and pinion, hour wheel,
# and a bevel takeoff share the central hand arbor behind the skeleton dial.
gear spur mounted vertical 800 355 84 6.7 72 0 14 14 none
gear lantern mounted horizontal 800 355 28 2.2 12 25 42 42 none
gear spur mounted vertical 690 355 38 3.0 36 8 0 0 none
gear lantern mounted horizontal 690 355 18 1.5 10 40 -58 -58 none
gear spur mounted vertical 910 355 38 3.0 40 18 0 0 none
gear bevel mounted horizontal 800 470 38 3.0 32 12 0 0 none

# STRIKE / BELL TRAIN - a second great wheel drives a compact ascending train,
# warning sector, count wheel, bevel transfer, and fast fly governor.
gear spur mounted vertical 1350 540 96 7.7 96 6 -10 -10 none
gear count mounted vertical 1460 430 58 4.6 78 16 0 0 none
gear spur mounted vertical 1210 495 70 5.6 72 8 0 0 none
gear lantern mounted horizontal 1210 495 24 1.9 12 28 30 30 none
gear spur mounted vertical 1115 405 55 4.4 60 20 0 0 none
gear spur mounted vertical 1085 300 44 3.5 48 0 0 0 none
gear lantern mounted horizontal 1085 300 20 1.6 10 10 -48 -48 none
gear sector mounted vertical 1125 215 46 3.7 36 52 0 0 none
gear bevel mounted horizontal 1214 185 40 3.2 32 0 0 0 none
gear lantern mounted horizontal 1284 185 30 2.4 12 20 78 78 none

# PLAYER BRAKES - stopping one freezes its matching hand on the central face.
# Correctly stopped hands turn green; mistimed brakes turn red and can restart.
gear spur mounted vertical 380 720 54 4.3 40 30 28 28 hour
gear bevel mounted horizontal 800 725 62 5.0 36 140 52 52 minute
gear escape mounted vertical 1220 720 56 4.5 30 235 85 85 second

# Gameplay, labels, and the exit return to the player collision plane. The three
# background brakes remain operable through middleground interaction proxies.
layer middleground
label 650 64 CLOCKTOWER MASTER MOVEMENT
exit 1460 620 80 200
